#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171893 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/id #uuid "61c3506a-5e4e-557f-bb8c-077170e93204" :question/math-academy-id "e-9468" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3?$\n\n- $\\mathbf R(x,y,z) = 2\\,\\mathbf i - x\\,\\mathbf j + y\\,\\mathbf k$\n\n- $\\mathbf S(x,y) = 2x\\,\\mathbf i - y^3\\,\\mathbf j$\n\n- $\\mathbf T(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{x}{z}\\,\\mathbf i - \\dfrac{y}{z}\\,\\mathbf j + \\dfrac{z}{2}\\,\\mathbf k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of $\\mathbb R^3.$ A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ is a function $\\mathbf F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $\\mathbf R(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z) \\in \\mathbb{R^3}$ to a vector in $\\mathbb{R^3}.$\n\n- The function $\\mathbf S(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$).\n\n- The function $\\mathbf T(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3\\:|\\: z \\neq 0\\big\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546232 :question-generator/id #uuid "ec85d8ee-287f-57d5-a57d-bc074f08815d" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186172087.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "257efe5e-2614-5ac2-bf85-79ecbfa90a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437600} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6b7630-7b4f-55f1-bc9a-d761bb022686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "257efe5e-2614-5ac2-bf85-79ecbfa90a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437600} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7b4231-7e44-5469-8d42-537ade15949a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2a1f4d6-a1e4-52e9-8825-2408433db854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437602} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b41f11-8dd8-570a-b746-ce040d0c6094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2a1f4d6-a1e4-52e9-8825-2408433db854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437602} :answer-field/id #uuid "666ed197-24fa-5d30-ae83-a374aabe3407" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2abe03-84b2-5689-9957-2c5ddaaeaf0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437604} {:answer/id #uuid "4235aad1-8567-5a5f-b358-a0eadb4ecae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4235aad1-8567-5a5f-b358-a0eadb4ecae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437605} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a3877a7-32e1-5f78-bf7a-c67ae72c6830" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "060c20fc-1491-5624-9b50-89ab0dfe4d22" :question/math-academy-id "q-122467" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $G(t)={e}^{t}\\,i-t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$\n- **II.** $H(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- **III.** $K(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $G(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x\\ne n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "662120df-b64d-54ef-9755-4c19a2619b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437690} {:answer/id #uuid "5f979ab0-c9f1-5a39-8279-36823d8a4b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f979ab0-c9f1-5a39-8279-36823d8a4b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437691} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a1bfb0-97af-571d-8fa7-cabca9f81b58" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438874} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68c998f6-9652-545f-9f75-a13c62365a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437692} {:answer/id #uuid "b439a47b-3c58-5ada-b83b-cb0d5f96aba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c998f6-9652-545f-9f75-a13c62365a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437692} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e0a766-53e1-58da-b795-ea4aa130a9a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a15fd7a1-495c-5a1f-9e2c-3e2cf8f73c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437694} {:answer/id #uuid "c163aff7-0957-5238-8912-1448c3c67129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a15fd7a1-495c-5a1f-9e2c-3e2cf8f73c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437694} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec68c1f1-2b47-5081-9d50-db69af906f2a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4052d0d0-adca-5eb3-9bef-49295b1e5651" :question/math-academy-id "q-122697" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $U(x,y,z)=⟨x+2,\\sqrt{x-y},\\operatorname{ln}⁡z⟩$\n- **II.** $V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$\n- **III.** $W(t)=⟨{t}^{2},2t,2-3t⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x\\ge y,\\,z>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $W(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b794e8c-8662-57a3-9430-d2ee2d5efdaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437648} {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649} :answer-field/id #uuid "616c4d45-069a-5832-84ae-5f981fb6e66f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51aecfc3-403e-5cba-b3b7-254b2d3ff5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437650} {:answer/id #uuid "1bb91534-359e-56df-b8a5-