unction $U(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a596d75-c886-5b2a-91fb-fb7040912254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437660} {:answer/id #uuid "14d600f9-2df6-53a0-baaf-26570d859584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14d600f9-2df6-53a0-baaf-26570d859584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437661} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfc827e-4a82-5cd1-a5ae-5c66a06116d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "660dc541-8ade-5251-99f2-6387f6ee265f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437662} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8b8c9c-d9b9-56b4-b891-4ed17c9de49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "660dc541-8ade-5251-99f2-6387f6ee265f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437662} :answer-field/id #uuid "028c2887-4e28-5453-a433-e92b6b42deee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91914c88-1e9a-57db-9467-36862e8b8bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437664} {:answer/id #uuid "602a7c8d-0df8-5802-a275-63a5f0ec8f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "602a7c8d-0df8-5802-a275-63a5f0ec8f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437665} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a0ad93-ccff-5c53-b92c-06f494f55cfe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09fffcb2-a27e-5da4-b160-3d4f79d02cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-122688" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D(x,y,z)=5\\,i+{z}^{2}\\,j+(y+x)\\,k$\n- **II.** $E(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-\\sqrt{y}\\,j$\n- **III.** $G(x,y,z)=x(y+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y-z)\\,j+{z}^{3}\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $D(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $G(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,y-z\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50d9f8ec-d2f4-53f4-a062-dd31da0e2d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437666} {:answer/id #uuid "95f89107-ff18-5c78-aa80-9d8bf74cb537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50d9f8ec-d2f4-53f4-a062-dd31da0e2d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437666} :answer-field/id #uuid "44c8354e-64c2-5521-9c4f-6fc0875dab62" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a67cd97f-b350-51ca-9d88-f274e517f2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437668} {:answer/id #uuid "dd39dffa-7a6e-5361-9525-4a0eb3d64ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd39dffa-7a6e-5361-9525-4a0eb3d64ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437669} :answer-field/id #uuid "1205eb0b-9fba-5a6b-a549-686ad592c413" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce5c525b-d1fc-5b97-8265-bcc663f447e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437670} {:answer/id #uuid "c9af1564-eb68-5d27-8c3d-f9f70675660d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce5c525b-d1fc-5b97-8265-bcc663f447e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437670} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7621621-f6bc-55f4-afc8-32adaf42a91d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d3cf160-5814-5830-a8cc-6fc64892cdce" :question/math-academy-id "q-122691" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $U(x,y,z)=(x+2){e}^{yz}$\n- **II.** $V(x,y,z)=⟨5{e}^{-{z}^{2}},{x}^{3}y,1-{y}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd70e4d-6c48-57c7-9de7-29fb91ecd156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437672} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a035b0-a3e5-53be-a422-6c7151b90283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd70e4d-6c48-57c7-9de7-29fb91ecd156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437672} :answer-field/id #uuid "82f16859-809f-5571-9e24-04024074834c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84952cf5-bae9-566b-8785-0e7b44cb9f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437674} {:answer/id #uuid "9499395a-41a6-544d-ae0b-b638a3373619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9499395a-41a6-544d-ae0b-b638a3373619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437675} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a42706-0e2c-5b8a-a048-2ec4e31f3fbc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df7e1c2f-9a73-51cd-b44a-97d3a3f06124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437676} {:answer/id #uuid "0039b744-c30f-5b87-90ae-3f6e231319ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0039b744-c30f-5b87-90ae-3f6e231319ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437677} :answer-field/id #uuid "28d18e6e-3fdd-511d-adcf-4ebf4d97e428" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "659f4527-cc88-5c6b-8485-f595eee1689f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122694" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $N(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},\\sqrt{x+y}⟩$\n- **II.** $P(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x-2y},\\sqrt{3-x},3{z}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $Q(x,y,z)=⟨-1,2,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x-y+z)⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $P(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,3-x\\ge 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,2x-y+z>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "381ec827-a8d9-525e-879e-9867a01781c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437684} {:answer/id #uuid "49b34905-3523-5220-8445-649a78b38000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "381ec827-a8d9-525e-879e-9867a01781c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437684} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ab9680-7869-5328-9a15-6eba928afef1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e56ee0-4b15-585a-b00b-9c198815d5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437686} {:answer/id #uuid "8084195c-c80f-5724-a464-b4190c772af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87e56ee0-4b15-585a-b00b-9c198815d5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437686} :answer-field/id #uuid "f57b8a4e-6326-51ba-9d83-e214db0e9062" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9acb7596-f53f-56d2-b363-d2432bfdfc06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437688} {:answer/id #uuid "7cff525b-7dbd-51e3-9c41-4f3a63d8b105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cff525b-7dbd-51e3-9c41-4f3a63d8b105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437689} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee64c134-4670-5bcf-b390-f48716fc96b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89ed8a40-4bb8-5a40-9a2c-1bf03637a8bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-122696" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C(x,y,z)=\\frac{z}{x+y}$\n- **II.** $D(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3}-3,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y),7{x}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $E(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),\\operatorname{tan}⁡z,\\frac{1}{x-y}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $D(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x\\ne y,\\,z\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa463bcd-c692-5b2e-81fb-6edd382301d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437654} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0c189c-4360-5311-8733-688846ac83f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa463bcd-c692-5b2e-81fb-6edd382301d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437654} :answer-field/id #uuid "eec2a251-816b-560e-984e-218cc993a24b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7e53ee-c545-556b-8c01-71673e0ac9c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437656} {:answer/id #uuid "133f3ccd-0846-5c2f-8e29-aac997ab0c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "133f3ccd-0846-5c2f-8e29-aac997ab0c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437657} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e2fd0e0-3c93-53a1-8f8a-f97251928fc1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22acadb3-7ca8-5abe-ad3c-4d0f8a82b17b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437658} {:answer/id #uuid "bafa02fd-27b6-50a3-b21c-bc14c4e05eaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22acadb3-7ca8-5abe-ad3c-4d0f8a82b17b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437658} :answer-field/id #uuid "a898dd6a-8e9a-579f-bcba-72e40817966d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b17979a9-57b7-5c2d-8065-c277267e307e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122686" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$\n- **II.** $Q(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-\\frac{x}{y}\\,j+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,k$\n- **III.** $R(t)=\\frac{1}{t+1}\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,z\\ne -1,\\,y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91acbdcb-0819-512d-8f3a-8f5b18843d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437678} {:answer/id #uuid "c042a6b6-5fe6-5670-9ac7-c7152c415d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c042a6b6-5fe6-5670-9ac7-c7152c415d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437679} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ff1394-a615-59ad-bb26-46d4946b7591" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77a73f89-d276-53da-ba0d-e39074166f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437680} {:answer/id #uuid "83b30725-25b3-5535-9453-a881c12cb3ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a73f89-d276-53da-ba0d-e39074166f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437680} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a11b4f3-6da8-5671-9b65-64280b7f35aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c27113d-a2f3-54dd-a0fe-40e814f8066c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437682} {:answer/id #uuid "88e9a9b2-4f69-57eb-9973-f4cc63d15d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c27113d-a2f3-54dd-a0fe-40e814f8066c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437682} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6f83e16-f061-5b3d-ae8a-955bb9e63305" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "438dc864-2346-5ec7-8b61-791bfb4d3c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-122695" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $M(x,y,z)=⟨z-{x}^{2},3x+{z}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$\n- **II.** $N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$\n- **III.** $P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x+y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cc858a-bb26-5425-9e3d-889624a9d6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546146} {:answer/id #uuid "c154fa30-500a-5a4e-a923-f15ad6ed70af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546208}] :answer-field/correc