$\n- **II.** $B(x,y)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$\n- **III.** $C(x,y,z)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of $\\mathbb R^3.$ A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $B(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ to a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0184f2ee-4e64-5c2a-8a40-b61e3bd221b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546132} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6d71c8-cb33-5800-aa9d-ea28edf26cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0184f2ee-4e64-5c2a-8a40-b61e3bd221b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546132} :answer-field/id #uuid "057fce37-626c-537a-b118-349f95fd6a41" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73f01417-eb54-5707-aff0-ecd5cbfcfbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546172} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f48cdf-de4b-5910-8e61-