bb R^3?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(x,y,z)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$\n- **II.** $B(x,y)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$\n- **III.** $C(t)=\\langle 2t, t^2, 1\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of $\\mathbb R^3.$ A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ to a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1974861-f207-5cae-b9f0-eb04b2136c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546201} {:answer/id #uuid "d2afa0da-cd53-525f-8352-357c203431e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1974861-f207-5cae-b9f0-eb04b2136c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546201} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe4f713-a18a-56ea-bc6d-54f9527a3306" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19bd4502-320a-5b01-bd50-cae3e702bde9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/