or in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\n- The function $B(t)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ to a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ad7ba9-81ac-553e-8ffe-37a112345fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546179} {:answer/id #uuid "fd521762-6972-57ec-95f0-1451ab5b98af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89ad7ba9-81ac-553e-8ffe-37a112345fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546179} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c0fe7d5-e70f-5fd0-bf52-7f99dc2c2868" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "574d6fbb-c23f-5ba8-9ac2-6cbde1b780dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546159} {:answer/id #uuid "6feafc39-2b77-5980-966f-9bfc3a31d279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6feafc39-2b77-5980-966f-9bfc3a31d279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546168} :answer-field/id #uuid "95ec8f76-2b4b-5fda-a746-6ac25299b3c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546188} {:answer-field/choices [{:an